# Seat: Interaction and states — Round 7 (working notes, written as I go)

Build: commit 984a0f17, frozen. Read the 119 ok() assertions in
interaction-check.mjs and the paid-for defect library first; both are
excluded from my findings.

## Log

- Tab order @1440 tasks.board: 18 stops, roving at rail (1 stop), view
  switcher (1 stop), card grid (1 stop + 4 in-card controls), Add row.
  Arrows walk all 5 lanes and every card; the empty `waiting` lane is
  skipped rather than trapping. No console errors. Home/End are no-ops
  inside the card rover (minor, not filed).
- `.cardDots` ("Move this task") is opacity:0 at rest, revealed by
  :hover/:focus-within, forced to opacity 1 under `pointer: coarse`, and
  its slot is reserved in layout so revealing it moves nothing. This
  class is closed — not a finding.
- Carry model verified live: Space announces "Picked up …", arrows
  announce "In progress, position 1 of 4.", Escape cancels and announces
  "Move cancelled. … is back in the to do column." and the card really
  returns to `todo`. This is award-level; nothing to file.
- CANDIDATE (parked): `timeline.loading` reserves a 372x372 card and the
  arrival is 372x1653 at 390, 1242x854 at 1440. The skeleton draws the
  horizon head only — no reserve at all for the measure, which is the
  organising object. Not a declared state and not shot, so weighed for
  scope before filing.
